    "https://emmanuel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206196": {
      "title": "Director of Academic Technology and Innovation",
      "description": "Emmanuel College\nJob Posting: Director of Academic Technology and Innovation Emmanuel College \n\tJob Posting: Director of Academic Technology and Innovation Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Academic Technology and Innovation Category: Information Technology Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Information Technology Locations: Boston, MA Posted: Oct 27, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 206196 Share About Emmanuel College: Emmanuel College is a co-educational, residential institution with a 17-acre campus in the heart of Boston's educational, scientific, cultural and medical communities. Enrolling more than 2,200 undergraduate and graduate students, the College provides boundless opportunities for students to expand their worldview through rigorous coursework, significant internship and career opportunities throughout the Boston area and beyond, collaborations with distinguished and dedicated faculty, and participation in a dynamic campus community. Emmanuel's more than 50 programs in the sciences, liberal arts, business, nursing, and education foster spirited discourse and substantive learning experiences that honor the College's Catholic educational mission to cultivate the whole person and prepare students for effective and ethical leadership in the 21st century. For more information, visit www.emmanuel.edu. Job Description: The Director of Academic Technology and Innovation: Acquires, evaluates and maintains a suite of e-Learning tools and academic software that support excellence in teaching and learning at the College; In consultation with Associate Dean, plans and oversees academic technology budget, negotiates and administers contracts for LMS and related SAAS; Provides leadership in building faculty development programs in the areas of teaching strategies, instructional design and educational innovation and participates actively in developing faculty knowledge and skills; Supervises a team that supports faculty in their use of the LMS (currently Canvas) and other learning technologies; Oversees the \"DiscoveryLab,\" a community makerspace. The Director also works closely with other Learning Commons staff, especially research librarians, to provide seamless, individualized support to all College instructors. The Director is responsible for communicating with key academic staff including department chairs and deans to provide tailored resources to the faculty and will track and integrate as appropriate emerging trends in technology, best practices, course design, and curriculum development. Requirements: Our ideal candidates will  have a Master's degree in Instructional Design, Instructional Technology or a related field.  Candidates should also possess at least five years of experience, preferably in higher education.  Supervisory and classroom teaching experience is strongly preferred. Additional Information: Emmanuel College seeks to create a working and learning environment that reflect the society and community in which we are located, and we actively encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. The posted salary range reflects the good-faith compensation estimate for this position. The actual pay offered will be based on the candidate's skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity factors.  $105,000-120,000. Application Instructions: After submitting your resume with this application form, you will be prompted to complete an Applicant Profile where you will be able to upload your cover letter and list of references. In order to be considered for this position, you need to submit all three documents: a resume, cover letter and a list of three references with phone numbers. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Emmanuel College 400 The Fenway, Boston, MA 02115"
    },
    "https://emmanuel.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206563": {
      "title": "Director of Major Gifts",
      "description": "Emmanuel College\nJob Posting: Director of Major Gifts Emmanuel College \n\tJob Posting: Director of Major Gifts Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Major Gifts Category: Development/ Research/ Public Relations Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Development and Alumni Relations Locations: Boston, MA Posted: Nov 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 206563 Share About Emmanuel College: Emmanuel College-a Catholic, coeducational, residential, liberal arts and sciences college in Boston-has been educating critical thinkers, ethical decision makers and community leaders since 1919. Situated in Boston's Fenway neighborhood within the Longwood Medical and Academic Area, Emmanuel's 17-acre campus is home to nearly 2,000 undergraduate and graduate students. The College provides boundless opportunities for students to expand their worldview through rigorous coursework, significant internship and career opportunities throughout the Boston area and beyond, collaborations with distinguished and dedicated faculty, and participation in a dynamic campus community. Emmanuel's more than 70 programs in the arts, humanities, education, natural sciences, business and nursing foster spirited discourse and substantive learning experiences that honor the College's commitment to educate the whole person and prepare students to emerge as tomorrow's leaders. For more information, visit www.emmanuel.edu. Job Description: As a key member of the Advancement team, the Director of Major Gifts will play a central role in expanding the culture of philanthropy at Emmanuel College by identifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding alumni, parents, and friends of the College. Working closely with the Vice President of Advancement, President, trustees, faculty, campus leaders, and Advancement team members, the Director will secure significant philanthropic investments that advance the College's strategic priorities and mission. The position manages a portfolio of approximately 125 prospects and donors and is responsible for securing leadership-level philanthropic commitments through annual, major, and planned gifts. 85% Frontline Fundraising & Portfolio Management Manage a portfolio of ~125 major gift prospects. Engage in personal outreach, cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship activities to advance donor relationships and secure outright gifts of $10,000+ and multi-year pledges of $25,000 to $1,000,000+. Conduct 12 or more substantive donor visits (in-person or virtual) every month. Execute a disciplined and active prospect outreach strategy including personalized meeting invitations by email or phone in addition to general prospect cultivation and stewardship outreach. Solicit and secure estate commitments from major gift prospects and others who have the ability to make a planned gift. Make 20+ major gift solicitations by the end of year 1. Raise a minimum of $500,000 in cash annually from the assigned portfolio. Continuously qualify and prioritize prospects, including alumni, parents, foundations, and others, to ensure a dynamic and productive portfolio. Develop customized solicitation strategies and write compelling gift proposals and correspondence. Develop and implement stewardship plans, including writing stewardship letters and reports for major gift prospects. Engage with donors outside of the assigned prospect pool to support the overall goals of the Emmanuel Fund annual giving program. Travel regionally and nationally as needed (approximately 30% of time); evening and weekend work may be required. 10% Collaboration, Events & Institutional Engagement Collaborate with team members, senior leadership, faculty, coaches, and administrators to align donor interests with institutional priorities. Partner with trustees, reunion volunteers, campaign volunteers, and key alumni leaders to advance donor relationships and philanthropic support. Plan and implement stewardship and cultivation events, effectively collaborating with colleagues, volunteers, and event hosts. Represent Emmanuel College at donor events, alumni gatherings, and other advancement activities. 5% Administration & Reporting Maintain accurate and timely records of donor interactions, strategies, proposals, and next steps within the College's donor management system. Assist the Vice President of Advancement with special projects as needed. Complete administrative reporting, travel planning, and related advancement documentation. Requirements: The ideal candidate will take an entrepreneurial and relationship-driven approach to major gift fundraising and demonstrate strong written and interpersonal communication skills. A deep commitment to Emmanuel's mission and collaboration across academic departments, athletics, mission and ministry, and institutional leadership is essential to drive results that align with College-wide priorities. A Bachelor's degree is required along with at least seven years of professional fundraising experience. Candidates should also have knowledge of, and experience with planned giving strategies.  Experience in higher education and an advanced degree are a plus. Additional Information: Emmanuel College seeks to create a working and learning environment that reflect the society and community in which we are located, and we actively encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. This is primarily an on-campus role. Following an initial onboarding period, there will be an opportunity for a hybrid work arrangement, based on the needs of the position and the College. Employees are expected to maintain a regular on-campus presence. The posted salary range reflects the good-faith compensation estimate for this position. The actual pay offered will be based on the candidate's skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity factors.  $100,000-130,000 Application Instructions: A complete application must include a cover letter, resume, a statement of purpose, and contact information for three references. In your statement of purpose, please describe how your values, experiences, and professional goals align with Emmanuel College's mission to educate and inspire in a diverse, inclusive environment. We encourage you to highlight your contributions to diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging in previous roles, as well as your vision for supporting Emmanuel's inclusive and collaborative community. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Emmanuel College 400 The Fenway, Boston, MA 02115"
    }
  },
